R&C patch 7108: the fragment-program decompiler gives WPOS.w as 1/w (the RSX value), not the host's clip w.
Idea from Re-TeRo17/ps3recomp 26ecf1a libs/video/rsx_fp_decompiler.c (MIT); a hand rewrite on our _rsx_wpos/_rsx_inv_w helpers.

Problem: WPOS (input 0) reads `_rsx_wpos(input.position)`, and the macro passed SV_POSITION.w through: (p).w in the
buffered (window-convention) form, (p) itself unbuffered. Under FXC (D3D12) SV_POSITION.w is the clip-space w; the RSX,
like GL's gl_FragCoord.w and NV_fragment_program's fragment.position.w, gives 1/w. The same file already knew this for
perspective_corr texcoord reads (_rsx_inv_w: 1.0 / w under FXC, the bare w where glslang lowered it to FragCoord.w and
RSX_FRAGCOORD_W_IS_RCP is defined), but WPOS did not use it, so on our D3D12 path a program that scales by WPOS.w was
off by w^2 while the Vulkan/Metal paths were right. Re-TeRo17's Tools of Destruction 1.2.1 fixed the same read in
their fork: Kreeli Comet's ground fog divides WPOS.w by the scene depth read back as colour and drew as an opaque
light-blue sheet with w in place of 1/w.

Fix (libs/video/rsx_fp_decompiler.c): _rsx_wpos takes its w from _rsx_inv_w(p) on both branches (buffered: x, y with
the window origin and pixel-centre bias as before, z, _rsx_inv_w(p); unbuffered: float4((p).xyz, _rsx_inv_w(p))), and
the _rsx_inv_w block is emitted when the body uses either helper. RSX_FRAGCOORD_W_IS_RCP keeps its meaning: the
glslang paths still read the bare FragCoord.w, now for WPOS too. Programs that do not read WPOS stay byte-identical;
programs that do get the helper block (new pipeline keys for those only). x, y, z and rsx_fp_apply_wpos_grid are
unchanged. No A/B switch: the decompiler's output feeds the pipeline cache and translator id.

Tests: libs/video/tests/test_fp_decompiler.c expects the new macro text and the helper with a WPOS read (90/90; the
tree without this patch: 4 failed). port/rc/tests/run_fp_wpos_w_test.sh: text checks for MOV r0, WPOS and WPOS.wwww
buffered and unbuffered, then the emitted helper macros evaluated as C for FXC (SV_POSITION.w = 4) and glslang
(RSX_FRAGCOORD_W_IS_RCP, FragCoord.w = 0.25): WPOS.w = 0.25 in all four. Without this patch: 12 text failures and
WPOS.w = 4 on both FXC forms (the glslang forms were already right).

Not checked in a game run: no WPOS.w-reading program has been identified in our titles yet (look at ig fog shaders).

